{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>To distinguish.</b> Not only one who is expert, but that one should know and recognize and be skilled in them (Sifra)." "<b>Between the unclean and between the clean.</b> Must one say between a donkey and a cow — and are they not already explicitly stated? Rather, between what is unclean to you and clean to you — between one whose windpipe was half-slaughtered and one whose majority was slaughtered." "<b>And between the living creature that may be eaten.</b> Must one say between a gazelle and an arod — and are they not already explicitly stated? Rather, between one in which signs of treifah developed rendering it kosher and one in which signs of treifah developed rendering it disqualified (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:02.311446635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}